Description: GLX takes zink through DRI3, not kopper, while the compositor announces stereo content
 Kopper, zink's own window system path, has no second view of a window; zink
 through DRI3 has (patches 0004, 0027 and 0028). On a desktop where NVIDIA's
 Vulkan driver runs zink, the session had to set LIBGL_KOPPER_DISABLE=1 for
 every program, or an X11 program that asked for stereo got one view.
 .
 glx_kopper_enabled() decides for a screen: LIBGL_KOPPER_DISABLE set to 0 or 1
 decides as before, and unset it is no while the root window announces
 _KDE_NET_WM_STEREO_CONTENT_SUPPORTED 2 or newer. The route is named in the
 log (LIBGL_DEBUG=verbose). A desktop without a stereo compositor keeps kopper.
 .
 The decision is per screen, not per window: a screen is DRI3 or kopper.
 Kopper with two views (the packed-pixmap series kept outside the recipe,
 prototypes/kopper-stereo) would let a stereo window and a plain one share a
 screen; it reads the eyes back and uploads them, so it stays a prototype.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
